    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-business-analytics-anchorage-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics - Anchorage, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Business Analytics Assistant Professor of Business Analytics 533489 Anchorage, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 30 UAA Coll of Bus & Public Policy Add to favorites View favorites *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. The Department of Management, Marketing, Logistics, and Business Analytics in UAA's College of Business and Public Policy is seeking an Assistant Professor of Business Analytics to teach and mentor students in Business and Data Analytics courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels. You will conduct research in these fields, covering topics such as machine learning, data mining, and predictive modeling, while also contributing to the university and community through service. This full-time, tenure-track role requires a Ph.D. in Business Analytics or Data Science and is a 9-month appointment beginning in August 2027. UAA is a comprehensive public institution with a main campus in Anchorage, supported by community campuses and extension sites across Alaska. The College of Business and Public Policy is accredited by AACSB and offers BBA Degrees in Accounting, Economics, Finance, Management, Business and Data Analytics, and Marketing, along with MBA, MPA, and MPP Graduate programs, Associate degrees, and various Occupational Endorsement Certificates. The Assistant Professor of Business Analytics is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position in the Management, Marketing, Logistics, and Business Analytics Department at the University of Alaska Anchorage. This role includes responsibilities in (1) teaching, (2) research, and (3) providing professional service to the university, the profession/discipline, and the community. The teaching load is three courses per semester, beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in subjects such as Business Analytics, Data Science, and AI. A successful candidate should have expertise in teaching and research within Business Analytics, AI, and Data Science fields. The candidate should be capable of teaching advanced concepts and have a strong foundation in relevant technical skills, paired with effective teaching and communication abilities. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Business Analytics, or Data Science, is required. A Ph.D. fields such as Computer Science, Mathematics, or Machine Learning will also be considered if applicant has completed relevant coursework and/or has relevant industry experience. Candidates who are ABD may be considered if they provide evidence that degree completion will occur prior to the hire date. Ph.D. must be from an AACSB accredited institution. Non-business Ph.D. degrees must be from an institution whose business program is accredited by AACSB or from a program accredited by an association comparable to AACSB (e.g., ABET). Preferred Experience: Relevant industry experience in Business Analytics, AI, Data Science, or related fields. Completion of relevant coursework in Business Analytics, AI, Data Science, or related fields. Position Details: This position is located on the UAA campus in Anchorage. Applicants must be able to relocate to Anchorage, Alaska by the position start date. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track, faculty position complete with both a competitive salary and full employee benefits package . UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, faculty time off (FTO), 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental and vision care coverage. Faculty salaries are based on a variety of factors, including education and experience. Review of applicants will begin immediately. To ensure consideration, please submit your application by 11:55 PM Alaska Standard Time on November 20, 2026. Special Instructions to Applicants: *Applicants must submit the following materials: Cover letter outlining primary and secondary teaching areas and summarizing current and planned research; Curriculum vita; Contact information for three professional references, including names, telephone numbers, and email addresses; *Copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application; official transcripts will be required upon hire); and List of courses taught relating to Business Analytics, Data Science, AI, or related fields. ☎️If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact Abbie Shercliffe, CBPP HR & Faculty Services Coordinator, at aplampman@alaska.edu . This position is represented by United Academics-AAUP/AFT (UNAC). https://unitedacademicsak.org/ *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance in completing this application or during any phase of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu . The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. All employees at the University of Alaska are expected to uphold the highest standards of ethics and professionalism when conducting or engaged in university business. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/equity-and-compliance/docs/clery/UAS_ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.clery@alaska.edu . Recommended Jobs Communications Specialist Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chanc for Student Affairs . Medical Assistant Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF VC University & Student Advancement Make a Difference in Student Health at UAF\n\nJoin the Student Health and Counseling Center as a Medical Assistant and play a vital role in supporting the health and well-being of UAF students. This rewarding position offers the opportunity to work with a diverse, multicultural student population while gaining valuable experience across a wide range of clinical responsibilities.\n\nMedical Assistants report to the Associate Director of Medical Services and work alongside compassionate medical and mental health professionals in a welcoming, collaborative, and growing practice. This position is currently available, with full-time and part-time opportunities offered on 9-, 10.5-, or 12-month contracts, providing flexibility to support a healthy work-life balance.\n\nTo thrive in this role, you’ll bring a strong foundation in medical assisting, clinical experience, adaptability, and a commitment to providing inclusive, student-centered care. Comfort with telemedicine, a collaborative approach, and enthusiasm for professional growth will help you succeed as part of a team dedicated to the health and well-being of UAF students.\n\nIf you’re looking for a meaningful medical assisting opportunity where you can make a difference, expand your clinical experience, and be part of a supportive and growing team, we’d love to have you join us! Accounting Specialist Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Provost UAF College of Natural Science and Mathematics Academic and Research Business Office (CARBO) is seeking an Accounting Specialist to help support the financial backbone of our academic programs. This entry-level position will produce accurate reports, reconcile accounts, and assist faculty and staff with fiscal questions related to teaching and research activities. If you’re detail-driven and enjoy meaningful work in a student-centered environment, this is a great opportunity to build your skills and gain professional experience in accounting and financial administration. The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-health-sciences-anchorage-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences - Anchorage, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Assistant Professor of Health Sciences 533548 Anchorage, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 30 UAA College of Health Add to favorites View favorites The University of Alaska Anchorage Division of Population Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time assistant professor (non-tenure track) for our academic programs (e.g., undergraduate Bachelor’s in Health Sciences and graduate Master’s in Public Health Practice [MPH]). This faculty position is responsible for advancing teaching and service in addressing public health issues in Alaska. Faculty may also engage in research, scholarship, or applied / community-engaged work depending on interests and workload. The anticipated start date for this position is Fall 2027. As a faculty member in the University of Alaska Anchorage (UAA) Division of Population Health Sciences (DPHS), the person in this role will teach an array of courses across both undergraduate and graduate programs and contribute to the academic and professional development of our students. We seek candidates with experience in health sciences, public health, health care, community health, or a related field who are prepared to teach in hybrid, online, and in-person environments. Faculty may also contribute to curriculum development, student mentorship, and other activities that support our academic programs. Faculty members will work independently and collaboratively with colleagues to produce high-quality teaching, student mentorship, and service, with opportunities to engage in research and scholarly activity that benefits Alaskans. Successful applicants who wish to maintain an active research or scholarly agenda may have opportunities to incorporate research, applied scholarship, or community-engaged work into their faculty workload. Recognized by the Carnegie Foundation as a Community-Engaged institution, UAA is a comprehensive university consisting of a main campus in Anchorage and several extension sites. As an open-enrollment university, UAA has a unique student-centered mission. Many of our students are first-generation college students who come from historically marginalized groups. The UAA community celebrates a rich cultural heritage and diverse student body. The DPHS has an undergraduate BSHS degree with both Pre-Clinical and Health Educator tracks, an MPH program, an Occupational Endorsement Certificate (OEC) in Gerontology, a Graduate Certificate (GC) in Public Health, and a minor in Public Health. The DPHS offers rich collaborative opportunities in our research centers, including the Healthy Aging Research Laboratory, the Center for Alcohol and Addiction Studies (CAAS), and as the Alaska Satellite Center for the Colorado Center for Diabetes Translation Research, where faculty engage communities in a wide range of applied health research projects to address some of our most pressing health concerns in our state, nation, and world. Please visit the UAA DPHS website for more information. The Division of Population Health Sciences (DPHS) strives to improve the health of all populations, especially those most vulnerable, by producing world-class public health and clinical scholarship, forging strong community partnerships, and educating the next generation of diverse health leaders in Alaska and beyond. Our faculty members assist UAA’s mission of transforming the lives of students and community partners through teaching, community engagement, research, and creative expression in a diverse and inclusive environment. Serving students, the state, and the communities of southcentral Alaska, UAA is a comprehensive, open-access, public university established on the ancestral lands of the Dena’ina, Ahtna, Alutiiq/Sugpiaq, and Eyak/dAXunhyuu Peoples. We particularly value candidates who are student-centered and committed to supporting students’ academic and professional development and/or who have experience working with rural, Indigenous, or Circumpolar communities. Minimum Qualifications: A Master's degree in a relevant discipline for faculty with little to no research assignment; a Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline for faculty with significant, ongoing research assignments. Preferred Experience: Doctoral/terminal degree in Public Health, Health Promotion, Health Behavior, a clinical health profession, or another field relevant to health sciences preferred. Position Details: This position is located on the University of Alaska campus in Anchorage. This is a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position with an expectation of in-person teaching in Anchorage, Alaska. The salary range is $66,462 to $80,000. Specific offers will be based on the candidate’s relevant academic preparation and experience. UAA employment includes a competitive full employee benefits package including retirement options, faculty time off, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental, and vision care coverage, and representation under a Collective Bargaining Unit. We review applications on a rolling basis. Because we may close the posting once a sufficient pool of qualified candidates is established, we encourage early submission. Please note that once a viable pool is identified, further applications may not be reviewed. To be considered, applicants must upload the following documents to their online application: Cover letter describing experience and credentials as related to the requirements of the position (required) Curriculum Vitae (required). Statement of Teaching Philosophy including a discussion of instructional philosophy and how you are prepared to instruct, mentor, and inspire a diverse student population (*required) . Applicants are also encouraged to submit an example of research, scholarship, applied practice, or other professional work relevant to the position (encouraged; not required). ☎️If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact Corrie Whitmore, Search Committee Chair, at cwhitmor@alaska.edu . *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. This position is represented by United Academics (UNAC). https://unitedacademicsak.org/ This position is term-funded and is reviewed annually for contract renewal at the University's discretion. The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance in completing this application or during any phase of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu . The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. All employees at the University of Alaska are expected to uphold the highest standards of ethics and professionalism when conducting or engaged in university business. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/equity-and-compliance/docs/clery/UAS_ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.clery@alaska.edu . Recommended Jobs Data Center Technician Fairbanks, Alaska, United States SW Office of Information Technology The Data Center Operations (DCO) group within the University of Alaska’s Office of Information Technology (OIT) is seeking a full-time Data Center Technician. The successful candidate will monitor the status of the UA’s statewide computer network, enterprise applications, hosted computer systems, and data center infrastructure, resolving or escalating any issues as needed. The Data Center Technician on duty maintains security of the state-of-the-art data center, monitors the building’s CCTV system, provides After Hours Service Desk support, and performs hardware installations. The successful candidate will be able to work shiftwork and overtime in a 24x7x365 data center, and must be comfortable working independently as part of a team. Current availability is for a swing-shift position, 4:00 pm - midnight. The option of moving to a different shift in the future would be based on seniority. Assistant or Associate Professor of Ecosystem Ecology Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Provost The Institute of Arctic Biology and the Department of Biology and Wildlife at the University of Alaska Fairbanks invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position in terrestrial ecosystem ecology relevant to boreal forest ecosystems. This is a 9-month (full-time) tenure-track faculty position with a 3-month appointment extension supported by external funding (if available). The position duties will consist of 40% teaching, 50% research and 10% service. Program Administrator Coordinator Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Research The Program Administrative Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for the Center for Transformative Research in Metabolism (TRiM), with the primary objective of reducing administrative burden on the Principal Investigator, Scientific Program Manager, Research Project Leaders, and other scientific personnel. The Coordinator maintains the organizational infrastructure required for a complex, multi-investigator NIH-funded Center and ensures that meetings, documentation, reporting, deadlines, communications, and follow-up activities occur efficiently and reliably. The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/term-instructor-or-term-assistant-professor-of-welding-anchorage-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Term Instructor or Term Assistant Professor of Welding",
      "description": "Term Instructor or Term Assistant Professor of Welding - Anchorage, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Term Instructor or Term Assistant Professor of Welding Term Instructor or Term Assistant Professor of Welding 533563 Anchorage, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 40 UAA Community & Technical College Add to favorites View favorites This position is responsible for teaching courses in the Welding Program. The Instructor is responsible for identifying and meeting the needs of the students, contributing to the curriculum development, and maintaining up-to-date knowledge of subject areas. The ability to work effectively with colleagues and students of various cultural and socioeconomic backgrounds is a must. Excellent written communication skills and computer literacy is required. This position requires knowledge and application of industry-accepted safety standards. The ability to demonstrate and instruct students in applicable theory and application of Welding outcomes is required. Teaching assignments are determined by college needs and the individual’s background and experience. A combination of academic and industry background equal to at least 2 years of experience is required. Previous experience teaching at the secondary or post-secondary level in a Welding or NDT related program is preferred. The ability to work effectively with colleagues and students of various cultural and socioeconomic backgrounds is a must. Excellent written communication skills and computer literacy also contributes to this position. Minimum Qualifications: Appropriate AWS certifications and industry qualifications are required for courses taught. An unrestricted Alaska driver’s license and clean driving record in compliance with UA Safe Driving criteria is required. AWS Certified Welding Instructor certification is preferred. An Associate of Applied Science degree in a field related to Welding & Nondestructive Testing Technology is strongly preferred. A Bachelor’s Degree in a related field is preferred. A combination of academic and recent work experience including relevant industry certification indicative of the ability to be successful in a faculty role may be considered. Position Details: This position is located on the University of Alaska Anchorage campus. This is a full-time, 9-month, term-funded, non-tenure track, faculty position complete with both a competitive salary and full employee benefits package . UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, annual leave, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental and vision care coverage. Faculty salaries are based on a variety of factors, including education and experience. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until a successful candidate is identified. Review of application materials will begin immediately. Search and selection procedures will be closed when a sufficient and viable number of qualified candidates have been identified. Please ensure the following documentation is submitted with your application: Cover letter CV Unofficial transcripts Contact information for three (3) professional references Please list and attach all relevant welding certifications (AWS, ASME, etc.) with your application submission. *Upload to Supporting Documents ☎️If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact Gregory Russo, Community and Technical College Welding Technology Department, at grusso@alaska.edu. This position is represented by United Academics (UNAC). https://unitedacademicsak.org/. This position is term-funded and is reviewed annually for contract renewal at the University's discretion. *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance with this application or at any stage of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu . The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. All employees at the University of Alaska are expected to uphold the highest standards of ethics and professionalism when conducting or engaged in university business. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/compliance/clery-act/annual-security-reports.html . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.orca@alaska.edu . Recommended Jobs Physical Access Control Systems Assistant Manager Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Admin. Services We’re looking for a motivated, detail-oriented, and adaptable Assistant Access Control Systems Manager to join our team! Accounts Receivable Specialist Anchorage, Alaska, United States UAA VC Administrative Services The Office of the Bursar at the University of Alaska Anchorage (UAA) invites applications for the position of Accounts Receivable Specialist. As a key member of our student‑facing team, you will play an essential role in managing current and past‑due student accounts and coordinating third‑party sponsorships. The Office of the Bursar oversees all university receipts and is committed to providing excellent customer service to students and external sponsors alike. If you have a passion for service, a strong eye for detail, and a desire to help students navigate the financial side of their college experience, this could be the perfect role for you. UAF Events Coordinator Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Chancellor * The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
